---@class posthog.conversations.ListConversationsTicketsRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field ai_triage_result? string Filter by AI triage outcome. Accepts a single value or a comma-separated list. Valid values: `persisted`, `suggested`, `escalated_with_findings`, `escalated_with_best`, `escalated_no_reply`, `skipped_unactionable`, `skipped_team_replied`, `skipped_channel_excluded`, `blocked_unsafe`, `blocked_unsafe_reply`, `clarified`, `suggested_clarification`, `in_progress`.
---@field assignee? string Filter by assignee. Accepts a single value or a comma-separated list (matches any, max 100 entries). Each entry is `unassigned` (no assignee), `me` (the requesting user), `user:<user_id>`, or `role:<role_uuid>`, e.g. `assignee=unassigned,user:123`.
---@field channel_detail? posthog.conversations.ListConversationsTicketsRequestChannelDetail|string Filter by the channel sub-type (e.g. `widget_embedded`, `slack_bot_mention`).
---@field channel_source? posthog.conversations.ListConversationsTicketsRequestChannelSource|string Filter by the channel the ticket originated from.
---@field date_from? string Only include tickets updated on or after this date. Accepts absolute dates (`2026-01-01`) or relative ones (`-7d`, `-1mStart`). Pass `all` to disable the filter.
---@field date_to? string Only include tickets updated on or before this date. Same format as `date_from`.
---@field distinct_ids? string Comma-separated list of person `distinct_id`s to filter by (max 100).
---@field emails? string Comma-separated list of email addresses to filter by, matched case-insensitively against `email_from` (max 100). When combined with `distinct_ids`, tickets matching either the distinct_ids or the emails are returned (OR).
---@field limit? number Number of results to return per page.
---@field offset? number The initial index from which to return the results.
---@field order_by? posthog.conversations.ListConversationsTicketsRequestOrderBy|string Sort order. Prefix with `-` for descending. Defaults to `-updated_at`.
---@field priority? string Filter by priority. Accepts a single value or a comma-separated list (e.g. `medium,high`). Valid values: `low`, `medium`, `high`, `critical`.
---@field search? string Free-text search. A numeric value (optionally prefixed with `#`) matches a ticket number exactly; otherwise matches against the customer's name or email, the email subject, or message content (case-insensitive, partial match).
---@field sla? posthog.conversations.ListConversationsTicketsRequestSla|string Filter by SLA state. `breached` = past `sla_due_at`, `at-risk` = due within the next hour, `on-track` = more than an hour remaining.
---@field snoozed? boolean Filter by snooze state: `true` returns only snoozed tickets, `false` only non-snoozed.
---@field status? string Filter by status. Accepts a single value or a comma-separated list (e.g. `new,open,pending`). Valid values: `new`, `open`, `pending`, `on_hold`, `resolved`.
---@field tags? string JSON-encoded array of tag names; returns tickets with ANY of them (OR), e.g. `["billing","urgent"]`.
---@field tags_all? string JSON-encoded array of tag names; returns tickets that have ALL of them (AND), e.g. `["billing","urgent"]`.
---@field tags_exclude? string JSON-encoded array of tag names; returns tickets that have NONE of them (NOT), e.g. `["escalated"]`.
---@field view? string Apply a saved ticket view's filters by its `short_id` (list views via the `conversations/views` endpoint). Any filter param passed explicitly overrides the view's saved value for that dimension. Returns 400 if no view matches.

